{%- comment -%}
  Three different refusals wear the same 403, and telling someone the
  wrong one sends them to argue with the wrong person.

  Someone with no agent record cannot reach support at all and needs to
  be added. An agent who walked into an Admin screen has access to
  support and needs to know it is this screen that is shut. An agent
  looking at a ticket in a department they do not cover is not being told
  about settings at all, which is what the middle message used to say to
  them.

  @param {object} [forbidden_entity] - The ticket it was asked about, if any
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  function agent = 'modules/support/helpers/current_agent'

  if agent == blank
    assign title = 'modules/support/authorization.forbidden_title' | t
    assign body = 'modules/support/authorization.forbidden_body' | t
  elsif forbidden_entity != blank
    comment
      There was a ticket in hand and the agent still failed the check, so
      the only thing it can be is the department.
    endcomment
    assign title = 'modules/support/authorization.department_title' | t
    assign body = 'modules/support/authorization.department_body' | t
  else
    assign title = 'modules/support/authorization.admin_only_title' | t
    assign body = 'modules/support/authorization.admin_only_body' | t
  endif
-%}
<h1>{{ title }}</h1>
<p>{{ body }}</p>
<p><a href="/admin/support">{{ 'modules/support/detail.back' | t }}</a></p>
